  <h2>How do the four buying models compare?</h2>

  <p>As models, not as companies. What differs is the unit you are charged for, which changes what a low number means.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Published managed design subscriptions state monthly floors between roughly $6,000 and $15,000, and the one card offering a named dedicated team starts at roughly $30,000 a month on a twelve-month term, plus a $1,000 monthly software fee.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: published subscription rate cards in this category, September 2026, published pricing pages only, no vendor named. The $30,000 dedicated floor appears on a single card.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Unlimited-request design subscription tiers run from roughly $700 to roughly $4,500 a month, month to month, with no capture, no talent and no usage included.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: published subscription rate cards in this category, September 2026, two independent pricing pages read directly.</p>

  <p>Two subscription bands, an order of magnitude apart, both called subscriptions. The cheaper one excludes capture, talent and usage, which is to say it excludes the three layers that make an asset a campaign asset.</p>

