  <h2>Questions buyers ask about cost per asset</h2>

  <h3>How much does one creative asset cost?</h3>

  <p>Published studio rate cards collected in September 2026 put a standard product image at $39 to $50, a model or lifestyle image at about $95, a short video clip at about $93 and a finished pro edit at about $199. Bulk ecommerce image editing runs far lower, roughly $0.25 to $1.20 an image, because it retouches an image that already exists rather than capturing one.</p>

  <h3>What counts as one finished asset?</h3>

  <p>There is no industry definition. This page uses one deliverable file, in one specified format and one specified duration or dimension, approved and cleared for its channel. Under that definition a resize, a language version and an alternate cut are each new assets, while an alternate take shot in the same session is not.</p>

  <h3>Why do agencies not publish cost per asset?</h3>

  <p>A per-asset figure exposes margin. The only published measurement of production transparency, from a US advertiser trade body in August 2017, found fewer than half of respondents required in-house bidding disclosure and more than 60 percent did not require rebates be returned. That study did not publish its own respondent count.</p>

  <h3>Is a subscription cheaper than a production studio?</h3>

  <p>It depends what you count. Unlimited-request design subscriptions publish tiers of roughly $700 to $4,500 a month with no capture, no talent and no usage included, while managed subscriptions publish floors of roughly $6,000 to $15,000. A subscription prices access to designers; production prices delivered assets. Compare them per delivered asset, not per month.</p>

  <h3>What does a cost per asset figure usually leave out?</h3>

  <p>Usage rights, most often. The US commercial production trade body's standard bid form itemizes a production across sections A to P and carries no line for media usage payments at all. Versioning and trafficking are the other two: under the performers' union agreement effective April 2025, an edit outside defined parameters creates a new commercial with new fees.</p>

  <h3>How much does a 30-second brand film cost?</h3>

  <p>No trustworthy published band exists for this at the finished-film level, which is why this page does not print one. The figures circulating are seller estimates without a sample or a method. What can be said from primary sources is that stills, social elements and behind the scenes are bid as separate budgets, so a film number and a campaign number are never the same number.</p>
